PrismJS 1.30.0 (vendored)
=========================

This directory contains a checked-in ESM build of PrismJS 1.30.0 used only by
assets/chat-highlight-worker.js. It is not an npm dependency, there is no build
step for it, and it is served from the same origin through the explicit asset
allowlist in src/http/handler.ts.

Files:

  LICENSE                 upstream MIT license, Copyright (c) 2012 Lea Verou
  VERSION                 PrismJS 1.30.0
  SHA256SUMS              sha256 checksum of prism-1.30.0.min.js
  prism-1.30.0.min.js     concatenated minified components, ESM default export

The bundle is the concatenation of these upstream components, in this exact
dependency order:

  core, markup, css, clike, javascript, markup-templating, typescript,
  jsx, tsx, json, yaml, bash, markdown, python, go, rust, sql, docker,
  diff, toml, ini, java, c, cpp, csharp, ruby, php, kotlin, swift, scala,
  lua, makefile, graphql, powershell

It starts with a provenance/license header and ends with:

  export default Prism;

Update procedure:

  1. npm pack prismjs@<version> in a temporary directory.
  2. Verify npm view prismjs@<version> dist.integrity matches the tarball
     before extracting. Never vendor a tarball from a non-registry URL.
  3. Extract package/components/prism-<name>.min.js for the component list
     above; confirm the dependency order is unchanged.
  4. Concatenate the components in order, prepend the license header, append
     "export default Prism;", and write prism-<version>.min.js.
  5. Run sha256sum on the new file, update SHA256SUMS and VERSION, and update
     the versioned path in src/http/handler.ts and the worker's dynamic import.
  6. Run npm test (checksum, size, ESM, and asset-serving tests) and
     npm run lint. Keep LICENSE verbatim.

Source and integrity for 1.30.0:

